--TEST--
there is no property-walk fallback: ordering two objects without `Comparable` is a compile error — `rule:classes/comparable`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Point {
    public int $x;

    public function constructor(int $x) {
        $this->x = $x;
    }
}
var $a = new Point(1);
var $b = new Point(2);
if ($a < $b) {
    echo "less\n";
}
// covers: lang:classes/comparable
// The marker sits at the end of the block: a line above the refused
// comparison would move the line number the expected diagnostic names.
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0411]: `Point` does not implement `Comparable`; ordering two objects with `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=`/`<=>` requires it
   --> case.nvs:11:5
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
